From d81a126c18ca5cd8a18feb89fcd762e2fe3ed451 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 14:29:09 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 40/41] venus: serve VK_KHR_pipeline_binary

The local protocol series gives the extension's five commands their command
ids and codecs, so the renderer can now dispatch them. Four are plain
forwards; vkCreatePipelineBinariesKHR creates objects and needs the renderer's
object tracking, because the guest names each VkPipelineBinaryKHR by an id it
chose and later destroys it by that id.

The command is unusual in two ways the dispatch has to respect. Its count is
in-out inside VkPipelineBinaryHandlesInfoKHR, and a driver asks how many
binaries a pipeline yields by passing no handle array at all, so a query
carries no object ids and must create nothing. And when the guest does offer
handles, the driver may fill fewer than it was given, so only the entries the
driver wrote become objects; the rest are released and returned as
VK_NULL_HANDLE. VK_INCOMPLETE is a success for this purpose: it means the
driver filled every handle it was offered and has more to give.

VkPipelineBinaryKHR joins the object handle union and the recognized object
types, and the device teardown path destroys any binary the guest left behind.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
